add('gsavln','results','PROTOCOL CHECK: Appendix A.2, PDF pp. 16–17, describes model-assisted benchmark construction: the speaker uses validation data during generation; candidate instructions are selected using DUET trained on other/unselected paths or two-fold cross-validation, and failed instructions receive GPT-4o visual correction. This construction conditions benchmark validity on a particular navigator and correction procedure. It is disclosed dataset construction, not by itself evidence that an evaluated navigator trained on its held-out answers. Controls should distinguish semantic validity, selector difficulty and the correction budget.')
add('m3e','results','PROTOCOL CHECK: Appendix A.1, PDF p. 14, splits episodes approximately 80/20 within each selected original val-unseen scene. Adaptation therefore receives labeled examples from the scene whose other episodes are tested. This evaluates supervised continual adaptation and within-scene held-out performance, not zero-shot transfer to scenes absent from adaptation. Table 5 has an internally inconsistent printed total and a small-scene row despite the stated exclusion; exact partition reconstruction is not established by the release.')
n['m3e']['implementation']='INSPECTED CODE, independently audited by assignment 05 at 35595353e6838b474ea835b9670419fa56e8f615: models/moe_lora.py:91–110 forms macro/micro softmax mixtures but evaluates all experts densely, unlike paper Top-K=2. tools/momentum/experts_stats.py:61–97,163 uses micro-only top-two counts and excludes near-tied pairs, rather than fused routing-probability workload in Eqs. 9–10. momentum_update.py:43–98 uses the intended new/old interpolation direction, with an extra frequency threshold; routers take new values. Visited-node representations are zeroed before macro routing (nav_model.py:171–192,261–267), although visited flags and topology remain. Alternating teacher/sample rollouts optimize supervised action CE, not policy-gradient RL (mp3d_agent.py:507–525,736–756). A compile-only test found import-star inside a function at nav_model.py:95; helper names also do not match definitions, and marco_router.py:28 unpacks a three-dimensional tensor into two shape variables. These are release blockers, not evidence that the authors ran this exact broken source. No cross-stage BWT/FWT aggregator or partition construction was located; FWT interpretation remains unresolved. The statistics launcher uses training data, not held-out labels. Full paths and inspection ranges: evidence/05/m3e_original_audit.md; static check setup/results: evidence/05/m3e_static_check.py and m3e_static_results.json. No fetched source was imported or executed.'
n['m3e']['repo_status']='Official source independently inspected by assignment 05; release blockers and paper/code discrepancies documented, with compile-only own test.'
